+| link:adr/0038-The_distroless_images_health_check_is_answered_by_the_application_binary_before_boot.adoc[ADR-0038]
+| The distroless image carries no executable other than the application itself, so its `HEALTHCHECK`
+  invokes that binary with a probe token which the entry point answers *before* the framework boots,
+  by a bare TCP accept against the compiled-in management port on loopback. The probe is
+  protocol-blind because the management scheme is deployment-bound
+  (link:adr/0025-The_whole_server-TLS_surface_is_neutral_in_gatewayyaml_and_bound_by_exactly_two_seams.adoc[ADR-0025]),
+  its logic lives in a separate testable class rather than in the untestable entry-point shim, and
+  the resulting health state is liveness -- readiness stays asserted where
+  link:adr/0031-Host-side_readiness_gates_derive_the_probe_URL_from_the_resolved_Compose_model_and_assert_readiness.adoc[ADR-0031]
+  puts it. *(Status: proposed.)*
